From 7c7ee467831227de1e61afe9406fb7f09880ca0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:39:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] patch 5: agent-side DPP Agent task

Add the agent-side DPP task and wire it into the slave thread:

- dpp_agent_task.{h,cpp} (new): DppAgentTask handles the wireless DPP
  relay proxy, wired extender enrollment FSM, and 1905-layer security
  (Network Introduction + 4-way handshake) for the agent.
- agent_db.h: new DPP structs/fields (dpp_extender_config, dpp_bootstrap,
  dpp_credentials, peer_1905_security).
- tasks/task.h: adds DPP_AGENT to eTaskType.
- capability_reporting_task.h/.cpp: publicizes
  prepare_ap_capability_message() for DppAgentTask's use building a
  spec-compliant BSS Config Request; sets the DPP onboarding capability
  bit when configured for DPP.
- ap_autoconfiguration_task.h/.cpp: branches the autoconfig FSM for
  DPP-onboarded agents (skips WSC M1, dedups chirp sends across
  multi-band radios, sends DPP_RADIO_INFO_NOTIFICATION in place of the
  WSC SLAVE_JOINED_NOTIFICATION).
- son_slave_thread.h/.cpp: registers m_dpp_agent_task and
  m_capability_reporting_task in the task pool, adds
  start_dpp_tcp_relay_server(), trigger_dpp_extender_bss_config_request(),
  and load_dpp_provisioned_keys().

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
